{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, everyone. I've called us together because we have a backlog of coated brackets, and the shared paint booth is available this weekend for a campaign to work through it. As Operations Director, I can authorize the campaign and set the operating controls, but before we can proceed, plant policy requires a documented operating plan — and that plan needs maintenance and environmental compliance sign-off before the first shift begins. So I need from this group: a draft operating plan for the weekend campaign, and sign-off from maintenance and environmental compliance. Let's start by hearing from maintenance and environmental on what they'll need to see in that plan."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to flag something before we go further. This morning I inspected the booth exhaust filter and measured the differential pressure at 2.4 kPa — that's above our 1.5 kPa maintenance limit. The replacement filter is in stores and takes exactly 4 hours to install. I haven't entered the reading in the maintenance system yet, but this needs to be addressed before any weekend campaign can run."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks, Jon — that filter reading is critical, and I agree it needs to be resolved before any campaign can proceed. From an environmental compliance perspective, I have some specific requirements I'll need to see addressed in the operating plan as well. I completed a permit review for this booth yesterday, and there are conditions that must be met before I can sign off. Rather than just listing them informally now, I think it's important that I formally put these on the record so they're captured in the campaign file. Let me do that now."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you, Jon and Priya. Jon, that filter reading at 2.4 kPa is clearly above our 1.5 kPa limit, so filter replacement has to be part of the plan — and with a 4-hour installation time, we need to schedule that maintenance window before the first shift begins. Please get that reading entered into the maintenance system and include the filter replacement as a prerequisite in the operating plan. Priya, I agree that your permit conditions should be formally documented in the campaign file. Go ahead and put those on the record now, and we'll make sure the operating plan incorporates every condition you list. Once we have Jon's filter replacement scheduled and Priya's requirements documented, we can assemble the full operating plan for sign-off. Let's hear Priya's formal requirements next."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you, Priya. Those three permit conditions are now formally on the record: 16 hours of operation, a VOC capture test at 95 percent or above before operation begins, and two certified coating operators assigned. Jon, we also have your filter replacement — 2.4 kPa reading above the 1.5 kPa limit, 4-hour replacement time, to be completed before the first shift. So the operating plan now needs to incorporate: one, filter replacement scheduled as a prerequisite before the first shift begins, with the reading entered in the maintenance system; two, a 16-hour operating window for the weekend campaign; three, a VOC capture test recording at least 95 percent capture before operation begins; and four, two certified coating operators assigned to the campaign. Before I can authorize this and we can finalize sign-off, I need to confirm: Jon, can you commit to completing the filter replacement — including entering the reading and scheduling the 4-hour installation — before the first shift begins? And Priya, once the operating plan documents all three of your conditions, are you prepared to sign off? I also need to know who will be responsible for scheduling and documenting the VOC capture test, and whether we have two certified operators available this weekend. Let's work through those items so we can assemble the final plan and get sign-offs completed."}
```

